title: DevShell Environment Implementation Plan
status: draft
created: 2026-11-07
author: adrian
approach: "The spec marks no requirement as an assumption. Every claim is a reading of the current contract, the prototype findings at adrs/2026-11-07-devshell-environment/findings.md, or the map evidence at maps/2026-10-31-nix-devshell-sandbox, so the plan builds against facts and returns no unresolved claim. Stage the change so the tree compiles at each step. First the contract: a generic ProvisionStep, the contribution types, Placement, SandboxAction, ResolvedStep and ContributionSupport, with Docker and TestBackend reporting empty contribution support. Second the registry and the generic step deserializer, so configuration parses a devshell step but preparation does nothing yet. Third host preparation: CommandRunner, checks, print-dev-env evaluation and closure. Fourth the resolver, orchestrator consent and preparation order. Fifth the doctor report. Sixth tests, arch-lint and documentation. The contract lands first because every consumer compiles against it. The one planning constraint is that no production backend applies contributions after this ADR: Docker refuses a devshell step, and linux-bwrap-provider and darwin-sandbox-provider consume the model later. The position and persistence tests therefore use the test backend and a child process of the test binary, and the host tests exercise the capture and the closure without creating a sandbox. One spec qualification follows from a fact the prototype recorded: FR-016 and AC-011 say the doctor creates no store path, while EC-008 says print-dev-env may write a flake source path on a dirty tree. The plan follows EC-008. The doctor creates no sandbox, workspace, branch or realised devShell, and on a dirty tree it reports the source write rather than claiming the store is untouched. A clean tree gains no path."
architecture: "### Module layout\n\n```text\nsrc/\n├── sandbox/\n│   ├── contract.rs       generic ProvisionStep, Placement, ContributionSort,\n│   │                     Contributions, ContributionSupport, ResolvedStep,\n│   │                     SandboxAction, CreateRequest.provision\n│   ├── environment.rs    StepProvenance.kind as a string; contribution rebasing\n│   └── selected.rs       capabilities derived from contribution support\n├── provision/\n│   ├── resolve.rs        sequence, settings validation, contribution support\n│   ├── kind/\n│   │   ├── mod.rs        Kind trait, KindDescription, SettingsError\n│   │   ├── registry.rs   the compiled-in table\n│   │   ├── command.rs    run setting and SandboxAction\n│   │   └── devshell.rs   installable setting\n│   └── prepare/\n│       ├── mod.rs        check and prepare entry points\n│       ├── runner.rs     CommandRunner trait and the system runner\n│       ├── checks.rs     nix, flakes, installable, validity\n│       ├── environment.rs print-dev-env evaluation, diff, six restores\n│       └── closure.rs    path-info -r and the store view\n├── orchestrator/service.rs  consent, prepare, request, preflight\n├── backends/docker/backend.rs  contribution_support empty; run SandboxAction\n├── cli.rs                doctor report with host checks and store view\n├── config.rs             generic step deserializer and store-view\n├── config_loader.rs      kind validation and store-view merge\n└── testing.rs            contribution-aware TestBackend and child-process test\n```\n\nThe registry is a table of `Kind` objects, each with a name, a placement, the contribution sorts it produces, whether it needs consent, a pure `validate` for settings, a read-only `check` for the doctor, and a `prepare` for create. The closed set of settings lives in `provision::kind`, not the contract. The contract carries only what a backend needs: where a step runs, the sandbox action to execute, and the contributions to apply. The resolver is still pure and I/O-free; it validates, checks contribution support and returns planned steps. Host preparation is the only module that spawns nix, and the orchestrator is its only caller. The doctor calls `check`, which runs the read-only queries, never `prepare`, so no hook runs and nothing is written.\n\n{{mermaid: architecture.mmd}}"
technologies[5]{name,role}:
  Rust,"The implementation language; standard library only for process, path and map handling"
  Nix,"2.34.9 or the host's version: print-dev-env for the script and output path, path-info for validity and the closure, --version for readiness"
  serde,"TOML for configuration and records, JSON for print-dev-env output; no new crate"
  tokio,"The existing async runtime; host preparation and doctor checks run on spawn_blocking so they do not block the reactor"
  arch-lint,"The repository's architecture rules; new scopes and deny edges for the kind registry and host preparation"
components[11]{name,purpose,details}:
  contract-types,"Give the backend a kind-free request and a contribution vocabulary","Replace ProvisionKind and the ProvisionStep enum with a generic ProvisionStep carrying identity, kind and a BTreeMap of settings. Add Placement { Host, Sandbox }, ContributionSort { Environment, Mount }, Contributions { variables, provenance, mounts, workspace_root, workspace_variables }, ContributionSupport { sort, state, reason, remedy, fallback }, SandboxAction { run } and ResolvedStep { identity, kind, placement, sandbox, contributions }. Replace CreateRequest.provision with Vec<ResolvedStep>. Change StepProvenance.kind to String. Add Contributions::environment_for(workspace) to build the runtime Environment and rewrite only the recorded workspace variables."
  kind-registry,"Own the closed kind set outside the contract","Add provision/kind with a Kind trait and a compiled-in table. Each Kind returns a KindDescription with its name, placement, contribution sorts and consent requirement, validates its settings, and exposes check and prepare. Keep an internal Parsed enum in the kind module for the settings; the contract never sees it. An unknown kind or an unknown setting fails with the identity and the kind. The command kind validates run and produces a SandboxAction. The devshell kind validates installable and produces contributions through the prepare module."
  host-preparation,"Check the host, capture the environment and derive the closure","Add provision/prepare. CommandRunner is a trait over process execution with a system runner and a recorded runner for tests. checks runs nix --version, print-dev-env and path-info without realising a devShell; print-dev-env may write a flake source path for a dirty tree, and the report says so. environment runs print-dev-env --json for the baseline and output path, then evaluates the print-dev-env script once in a bash child. The child starts from a caller environment with HOME, PATH, PWD, OLDPWD, SHLVL and _, dumps env -0 before and after, and returns the diff. Restore NIX_BUILD_TOP, TMP, TMPDIR, TEMP, TEMPDIR and terminfo to their before values. Keep exported-but-empty variables. Record the workspace root and the variables whose values contain it. Record a host path for a value that is a single absolute path outside the store and the workspace. closure runs path-info -r over the output path, or returns the store root for the whole view. check runs checks plus closure for the doctor. prepare runs checks, environment and closure for create."
  resolver,"Resolve the selected backend's sequence without I/O","Keep resolve and preflight_steps pure. Read each definition's kind from the registry, validate its settings, compare its contribution sorts with the backend's contribution_support, and return planned steps carrying the generic step, the kind description and the support entry. A missing sort is Unsupported naming the step, backend, sort, reason and remedy. A missing kind or bad setting is Misconfigured. The resolver no longer matches on a kind enum."
  orchestrator,"Own consent, preparation order and the request","In create, resolve, check consent for every step whose kind requires it, prepare every planned step on a blocking thread, then create the branch, stage the workspace and build CreateRequest. A preparation failure returns before the branch exists. The request carries ResolvedStep values in sequence order. Keep the doctor's preflight shared with create: preflight resolves and reports per-step outcomes, and a separate check_host step fills the host reports for the doctor."
  docker-backend,"Keep Docker's behaviour and refuse host contributions","contribution_support returns an empty list, so any step with a contribution is refused before create. create runs only ResolvedStep values with a SandboxAction, in order, and records the command steps' provenance. DockerData keeps container, forwards and Provenance. exec, inspect and delete are unchanged. The provision:command capability becomes no provisioning capability."
  doctor,"Report the kind, the host requirements and the store view","Change DoctorStep.kind to Option<String>. Add the contribution support entries, the store view and, for each host step, the requirement checks, the installable, whether it is valid and the closure count. Map a failed requirement to Unavailable with its reason and remedy. A devshell step in a project without consent maps to Denied. The doctor calls check, never prepare, and creates no sandbox, workspace or branch. Evaluation may write a flake source path on a dirty tree, and the report says so."
  config,"Parse the generic step and the machine-owned store view","Give ProvisionStep a custom deserializer that removes identity and kind and keeps the remaining keys in settings. validate_provisioning keeps the generic rules and calls the registry for kind-specific validation. Add StoreView { Closure, Whole } to Config, honoured only from the local override; a project value is ignored with a notice. Default to Closure."
  testing,"Prove the contribution model without a production backend","Make TestBackend's contribution support configurable and record the ResolvedStep values in the record. exec applies the recorded environment and mounts to the command it runs; inspect returns the provenance. Add a test-only third kind to the registry, behind cfg(test), which produces an environment contribution but has no contract variant. Add a child-process test: create a record with the test backend, write it through metadata_store, spawn the test binary with an environment variable, and assert the child reads the same environment and provenance."
  arch-lint,"Declare the new dependency direction","Split the provision scope into litterbox-kinds at src/provision/kind/**, litterbox-prepare at src/provision/prepare/** and litterbox-provision for the resolver. Allow config to reach kinds and prepare to reach kinds. Deny every backend the kinds, prepare and resolver scopes. Deny prepare the backends, orchestrator, surfaces, persistence, SCM and configuration scopes. Add a negative fixture for each new deny edge."
  documentation,"Document the configuration and the report","Add the devshell step, installable, store view and consent to the configuration reference. Document the doctor's host report with the existing preflight output. Add kind, contribution, host step and store view to CONTEXT.md. Extend the nix capability prompt with the print-dev-env evaluation and the six restores."
dataFlow: "The loader parses [[provision]] into a generic step, removes identity and kind, and keeps the remaining keys as settings. The registry validates the kind and its settings at load and rejects an unknown kind or key with the identity. The resolver reads the selected backend's sequence, asks the registry for each kind's placement, contribution sorts and consent requirement, compares the sorts with contribution_support, and returns planned steps. The orchestrator checks consent, then prepares each step on a blocking thread. A command step becomes a SandboxAction. A devshell step checks the host, evaluates the print-dev-env script once, restores the six nix variables, derives the closure and returns contributions. The orchestrator builds CreateRequest with ResolvedStep values in order and calls the backend. The backend runs the sandbox actions, applies the contributions and writes its own payload to SandboxRecord.data. Later exec and inspect calls read that payload, so a second process sees the same environment and provenance. The doctor takes the same resolver path, but calls check instead of prepare, so it reports the requirements, installable, closure count and store view without running the hook or creating anything."
deployment: "No new binary, service or dependency. The change lands in agentkit-litterbox and every in-repo consumer is updated with it. A project without a devshell step behaves as today. Docker refuses a devshell step with a structured Unsupported failure. No production backend applies the contributions until linux-bwrap-provider and darwin-sandbox-provider. Host preparation runs nix as a child process on a blocking thread; the doctor's checks do not realise a devShell and create evaluates the hook only after consent. The host tests require nix and a valid devShell and are selected separately from the unit tests, which use recorded output and never touch the network or build a derivation."
